dict(slug="wellness-real-estate-tulum", section="Wellness Real Estate", date="2026-10-21",
title="Wellness Real Estate and the Future of Luxury in Tulum",
desc="Wellness real estate reached USD 876 billion in 2025. What separates real wellness homes from wellness marketing in Tulum and the Riviera Maya.",
body="""We are becoming increasingly conscious of what we put on our bodies. But how conscious are we of the environments in which we live?

Jenny McCarthy's evolution from entertainment to Formless Beauty, a brand built on ingredient awareness and transparency, reflects a shift in consumer culture. It is also where beauty, wellness, hospitality and luxury real estate begin to intersect.

According to the Global Wellness Institute's May 2026 research, wellness real estate reached USD 876 billion in 2025, with projections of USD 1.8 trillion by 2030.

## What is wellness real estate?

The intentional design, construction and operation of living environments that support physical, mental and social wellbeing.

Imagine a home where natural light supports your daily rhythm. Where air quality, water management, acoustics and thermal comfort are fundamental architectural decisions rather than afterthoughts. Where wellbeing is not something you purchase during a vacation, but something your residence supports every day.

## Wellness marketing is not wellness real estate

- A jungle setting does not automatically make a building sustainable.
- A spa does not guarantee healthier living.
- A beautiful residence does not eliminate the need for environmental, legal and financial due diligence.

> For Tulum's next generation of luxury homes, credibility will come from measurable building performance, responsible development and lasting quality of life.""",
faq=[("How big is the wellness real estate market?","The Global Wellness Institute estimates USD 876 billion in 2025, projected to reach USD 1.8 trillion by 2030.")]),

dict(slug="longevity-the-next-luxury-pitch", section="Wellness Real Estate", date="2026-11-08",
title="Luxury Used to Sell Access. The Next Pitch Is Longevity.",
desc="The Estate by sbe and the shift of wellness from amenity list to operating model, and the accountability questions Tulum buyers should ask.",
body="""Sam Nazarian's latest move with The Estate by sbe is a useful signal for real estate: wellness is shifting from an amenity list toward an operating model.

The platform, associated with Nazarian, Tony Robbins, Marc Anthony and Richard Attias, announced branded residences in Coral Gables and Tampa and a resort-residential proposal at Playa Secreta in El Salvador. These are announced plans, with key details still undisclosed for the Florida projects.

## How the structure works

- Hospitality and brand-building from the operator.
- Visibility, networks and cultural reach from the celebrity partners.
- Project execution from local development partners.
- The service layer from longevity and wellness providers.
- Buyers asked to value the home and the ongoing experience together.

That last point changes the underwriting. When wellness is central to the proposition, buyers need to understand who will operate it, what services are guaranteed, what they cost, and how the brand relationship works over time.

## The Tulum context

Tulum already has a range of wellness-oriented propositions. The models differ, and public project descriptions should be checked against contracts, delivery status and operator commitments.

> The strongest question is not "How many wellness amenities are included?" It is: "Who is accountable for the experience after the property opens?" """),

